# TP Reviews Engine - Git attributes
#
# TR-BLD-002  .gitattributes MUST enforce `text eol=lf` for all text files.
#             A CRLF line ending in a JSON payload changes its bytes and
#             therefore its content hash, silently breaking hash-gating on
#             Windows checkouts.
# INIT-01     This is the first file committed to the repository. A file
#             committed before this rule may carry CRLF permanently.
# IR-07       Line-ending drift on a Windows development machine breaks the
#             byte-determinism that change detection depends on. The symptom
#             is a ~50x multiplication of commit churn, months later.
#
# Attribute matching is last-match-wins, so the catch-all is declared first
# and every override follows it.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts. `binary` is the built-in macro for `-text -diff`: these
# are never line-ending normalised and never diffed as text. Diagnostics
# screenshots must be stored byte-for-byte as captured. (IMPL PLAN 12.1)
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.woff2 binary

# Captured page fixtures are data, not source. Excluding them from language
# statistics keeps those statistics meaningful. (IMPL PLAN 12.1)
fixtures/**/*.html linguist-vendored
